  "body": "## Change and mathematical scope\n\nOn one historical PR626 JP8 block, defer a target halving through 55 additions, adjust every coefficient and pay restoration. Composed with credited PR751 equal-magnitude fan-in and identical known-zero work-clear elision, the backward block costs 135 -> 102 primitives per real component: **66 further real primitives**. The PR755 forward companion is checked too. No new kappa or global supplier improvement is claimed.\n\nThe backward local row-L1 peak doubles **109/4 -> 109/2**; denominator depth is unchanged. Complete provider precision, grouped interfaces, native admission and assembly remain open. This is a research note / finite scalar construction, not a precision-admitted supplier.\n\nThe restricted exhaustive census prices 221 starts and 557,559 intervals per orientation. Only the chosen witness receives endpoint/prefix replay. PR755/751 already beat the unshared witness; the contribution explicitly composes their equal-magnitude circuits. No superiority over PR830 varying-magnitude methods or PR975 X4 words is claimed.\n\n## Validation\n\n`python3 -I -B research/jp8-scale-intervals-seed35/verify.py`\n\nExpected: `PASS_JP8_SCALE_INTERVALS starts=221 intervals=557559_per_orientation backward_real_saving=66_beyond_equal_magnitude_fanin no_new_kappa`.\n\nSeparate dense Fraction implementation checks four block maps on all 57 arbitrary input columns, dirty work and helpers, every prefix, both clear-elision variants and 20 mathematical mutations. Nine package controls include optimized minimal offline relocation, actual source corruption, typed receipt corruption and boundaries. Eight exact source/base Git-blob bindings, optimized replay, selected-record integrity and whitespace checks pass on CPython 3.9.6/macOS arm64. Full repository/cold supplier suites, hosted CI and Lean were not run.\n\nExact base: bbc600db2fc15007b7c914f4f2b2ed55fa909c87. OS seed35, complex supplier track. Only research/jp8-scale-intervals-seed35/ is added; published tree equals the verified local tree. No pinned coordination issue existed; local claim records the result and branch link. Immediate pre-submission overlap refresh through #981 found distinct root-traversal work.\n\nCredit PR622/626 lineage, Sagar Thakrar PR696/751, Gareth Davidson PR837, Philipp/mightyOil PR882, PR839, taizaki69 PR755, Jeffrey Cox PR739, Ryan Haines PR830, Ross Richardson PR919, PR949 and retained predecessor notices. Prepared by Eva Ayala / ToikY with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance in mathematics, implementation, separate checking and writing. Apache-2.0; no independent human review claimed.",
